=== Round #5 — Transform, then Smoke while unrevealed ===
Input: keyPress T, wait 200ms, keyPress G.

Console:
  [V07-PROBE] RequestSmoke fired by Demiurgos_18, argCount=0
  (no [V07-PROBE-CLIENT] SmokeBurst line — see below)

Client readback:
  execute_luau (Client): #(_G.__v07_smoke_bursts) => 0

This matches src/server/Services/MonsterService.luau's validateAndSmoke (read at
MonsterService.luau:1603-1650): when CamouflageRules.evaluateSmoke(...) returns anything other than
"OK", the function just `return`s — no reply of any kind is sent, unlike RequestCamouflage which
always answers with a CamouflageUpdate verdict. So the correct signature of "refused, unrevealed" for
smoke is: the up-remote fires (argCount=0, confirmed), and NOTHING comes back — no SmokeBurst, no
verdict, no cloud instance. That is exactly what was observed.

search_game_tree (Server, keywords "smoke,Smoke,cloud,Cloud") after this round found no gameplay
instance under either name anywhere in the DataModel — only Roblox's own engine/stats items
(OpenCloudService, RenderBreakdown.Cloud, a ScriptDebugger named SmokeControllerDebugger — Studio's
own debugger UI, unrelated) and the two Remotes objects (ReplicatedStorage.Remotes.SmokeBurst,
.RequestSmoke). No smoke particle/cloud part was ever created, consistent with the burst list on the
server never having an entry.

=== Summary of the two negatives the coordinator asked to be the "actual point" ===
- workspace.AmbientLife held 16 models before, during, and after every refused Camouflage press
  across 5 rounds. It never moved.
- The player's own Character remained parented to workspace (playerCharacterInWorkspace=true) at the
  moment closest to the refusal that could be captured. The avatar never disappeared.

Both negatives held under a Transformed, forced-Aswang, unrevealed camouflage attempt, and under an
unrevealed smoke attempt. §4.3's gate did its job in every trial.
